# MoonlightWeb — environment configuration (copy to .env, never commit .env)
#
# .env is loaded at startup into the process environment (see main.cpp:loadEnvFile)
# and is also read at build time for the embedded fallback cert (CMakeLists.txt).
# All values below are OPTIONAL: without them the server runs perfectly well —
# on the LAN with a self-signed certificate, and from the internet through the
# rendezvous server, which needs no domain and no certificate of your own.

# ── Rendezvous domain ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Parent domain of the introduction server this build talks to. An instance is
# reached at https://stream.{MW_DOMAIN}/{rendezvous_id} — a held connection,
# not a published record: nothing is written to DNS and no port is forwarded.
# Leave unset to use the project's own (moonlightweb.top).
MW_DOMAIN=example.top

# Shared API key (X-API-Key) for the project's own services: the update relay
# and the aggregate metrics endpoint. Its presence is also what tells an
# official build from one you compiled yourself — without it, this binary never
# contacts our infrastructure at all. This is a SECRET.
MW_PDNS_TOKEN=your-api-key

# ── LAN-only development (forks) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1 = this instance reaches none of the project's servers: no rendezvous line,
# no STUN, no UPnP mapping, no update check, no census — and turning Internet
# Access on answers an error instead. Also set it in the environment CMake is
# configured from to bake it into the binary. See CLAUDE-LAN-DEV-SETUP.md.
# MW_LAN_ONLY=1

# ── Behind a reverse proxy ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The proxies (addresses or CIDR networks, commas or spaces) whose
# X-Forwarded-For / Forwarded headers are believed, so the clients behind them
# get their own rate limits, bans and line in the sessions list instead of all
# sharing the proxy's address. Bookkeeping only: it grants no access, and the
# admin page and LAN-only gates keep judging the proxy's own address. List the
# proxy's exact address; the proxy must APPEND to X-Forwarded-For (nginx:
# $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for). Set here, it wins over trusted_proxies in
# settings.json and the admin page shows it read-only. Unset = no proxy believed.
# MW_TRUSTED_PROXIES=192.0.2.10

# ── TLS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Nothing to set. On the LAN the server serves a self-signed certificate it
# generates itself; through the rendezvous the introduction server terminates
# TLS with its own.
#
# Bring your own domain + certificate (optional). Do NOT set anything here;
# instead, in settings.json set:
#   "domain":   "your.fqdn.example"            (a FQDN you own)
#   "cert_pem": "C:/path/to/fullchain.pem"     (file path)
#   "cert_key": "C:/path/to/key.pem"           (file path)
# cert_pem/cert_key accept either a file path or an env var name. Forwarding
# 443 to this machine is then yours to configure on your router — MoonlightWeb
# maps no web port of its own.
